From bd83a38c519b277537634f12180f624059e40dde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Janice <djanice1980@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 20:46:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: Gate HDMI FRL status polling on active FRL
 link rate

Backport of the upstream change of the same name (amd-staging-drm-next,
2026-08-04), which is not in 7.2.x.

hdmi_frl_status_polling_work() skipped every link whose connector_signal was
not SIGNAL_TYPE_HDMI_FRL. connector_signal is assigned once per link from the
connector type in link_factory.c and is SIGNAL_TYPE_HDMI_TYPE_A for an HDMI
connector; nothing in the tree ever assigns SIGNAL_TYPE_HDMI_FRL to it (only
stream->signal takes that value). The condition was therefore always true and
the 200 ms FRL watchdog never polled any link at all, on any system.

Confirmed empirically on 7.2.6 (Strix Halo, native HDMI FRL to an LG C2): with
a diagnostic print added inside hdmi_frl_poll_status_flag() and
drm.debug=0x2 for five minutes with a live 4K120 10 bpc FRL stream, not one
line was emitted -- the work runs but the loop body is never reached.

Gate on the active FRL link rate instead, as upstream does, so the watchdog
actually examines FRL links and can retrain when the sink asks.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
index 36982ca..27a466a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -2024,7 +2024,7 @@ static void hdmi_frl_status_polling_work(struct work_struct *work)
 		if (!dc_is_hdmi_signal(dc_link->connector_signal))
 			continue;
 
-		if (dc_link->connector_signal != SIGNAL_TYPE_HDMI_FRL)
+		if (dc_link->frl_link_settings.frl_link_rate == 0)
 			continue;
 
 		link_update = dc_link_frl_poll_status_flag(dc_link);
-- 
2.55.0

